structured.summary:
I rewrote feat.trd for FEAT-ZD-48600 in full, and the api:github refusal is fixed. The connector still fails (GITHUB_TOKEN is not configured), so it is no longer cited anywhere; the credentials problem goes to the step owner as TQ-12.

Every citation now resolves to a source read in this session: the three inputs, requirements/ZD-48600.md and shared memory.

The TRD contains:
- components affected;
- exact interface requirements for to_model, delays_by_vendor, vendor_risk, build_explanation_request, overdue_with_risk and renderOverdueRisk;
- the CT-1 JSON contract;
- data, security and tenancy sections;
- 13 tests, including the 30-day and 10-day boundaries;
- 10 risks;
- traceability to every PRD acceptance criterion and non-functional requirement;
- a decision-log check.

The code-level checks V-1 to V-8 go to the coding lanes and the Architect. No question is blocking.

